BUILT TILES carry the terms of what they are made from:

  - Archives derived from OpenStreetMap (the Protomaps extract, and osm.pmtiles): Open Database Licence
    (ODbL) 1.0, © OpenStreetMap contributors. https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/
  - Depths and relief wherever Natural Resources Canada's West Coast topo-bathymetric
    DEM has data (north of about 48.06°N): Open Government Licence – Canada.
    https://open.canada.ca/en/open-government-licence-canada
  - Depths and relief everywhere else near the coast, from NOAA's Coastal Relief Model:
    public domain.
  - Depths in the deep ocean, from the GEBCO_2026 Grid: public domain. GEBCO
    Bathymetric Compilation Group 2026, doi:10.5285/4f68d5c7-45eb-f999-e063-7086abc036fa
  - marine.pmtiles: names on the US side from the USGS Geographic Names Information
    System, and the boundary at sea from NOAA's maritime limits and boundaries, both
    public domain; names on the Canadian side from Natural Resources Canada's Canadian
    Geographical Names Database, Open Government Licence – Canada. Contains
    information licensed under the Open Government Licence – Canada.

Not for navigation.
